==Strategy==
Stall at the beginning, as a massive wave of Metal Doges, Gory Darks and Angelic Gories can quickly overrun any formation if given the chance, even with the enemy limit in mind. The Metal Doges will appear first, so take them out as quickly as possible or a Gory variant will get in the way. Paired with meatshields, a stack of DPS units will stun-lock the Gories, eventually winning the stage by pure attrition.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] - With low critical chance and rapid area attacks, Catornado is the perfect response to Metal Doges for most strategies as it can quickly whittle them down when protected well. With some luck, it can land a crit to kill them instantly, allowing the remaining units to focus on the Gory variants.
*[[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] - Catasaurus is probably the only viable critter on 4-crown, especially when talented for a maximum of 12% critical chance. While it relies heavily on luck, amassing a stack of them can still help to defeat the Metal Doges.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg]] - Cyborg is an accessible disposable midranger. One might not make too much of a difference, but when in numbers their repeated attacks will usually catch the Gories and force them away.
*[[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] - Ururun is one of the few helpful backliners, beating many others with her accessibility, long range, rapid attacks and 20% chance to cause knockback. She should be deployed in company of other units and catch enemies that manage to break past the frontline.
*Most surge units work in this stage, as long as they're good ones.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]] - In normal form, Kasa Jizo is an excellent midranger with rapid attacks that deal massive damage to Angels and Darks, trivializing the stage in its entirety once the Metal Doges have been taken down.
*[[Kasli the Scourge (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Scourge]] - Kasli's evolved form is able to annihilate this stage.

