==Trivia==
*''Rinrin'' (凛凛 or りんりん) is a Japanese word with a few meanings, including bitter cold, severe, intense, awe-inspiring, or the sound of a bell ringing. However, ''rin'' is also one way to read 林, meaning forest, and a [[wikipedia:Windbreak|shelterbelt]] is a line of trees and shrubs planted to shield an area from wind and lessen erosion; in Japanese, the word for shelterbelt is ''bōfurin'' (防風林), literally meaning "windbreak forest", so "Rinrin Bōfurin" essentially sounds like "Forest Forest Windbreak Forest".

